Requests

responsibilities

Building 
 - contain multiple floor

floor 
  - creates hall requests
  - have option to up and down clicks
  - call controller upon request

ElavtorController
     - respond to outside ruests + delegate to best elevator possible
     - response to inside request optimize to best next floor


Eleavtor
    -move bw floors
    -open/cose doors
    -mantain current floor
    -matain current direction
    -mantain current state
    - provide current state
    - set state
    -execute assigned requests
    -takes inside requests call controller



requests 
  - floor and up or down in each request
  - inside request to be one of destination floors



Core Entities Precisde

Building
- contains multiple floors
- contains multiple elevators

Floor
- has up/down buttons
- creates hall request
- sends request to ElevatorController

ElevatorController
- receives hall requests
- chooses best elevator
- assigns request to elevator
- tracks elevator status
- ignores elevators in maintenance

Elevator
- moves between floors
- opens/closes doors
- maintains current floor
- maintains current direction
- maintains current state
- maintains pending requests
- executes assigned requests
- accepts inside requests
- reports current status

HallRequest
- source floor
- direction (UP/DOWN)

CabinRequest
- destination floor

ElevatorAllocationStrategy
- selects best elevator for a hall request



relationships
buildings - floors,elevators
floors - has access to elevatorController to send requests
elevator - 



user flow
user enters building - could be any floor - create hall request
-enters elevator which arrives at floor - creates cabin request
-exists at desired floor


system flow
building(floor and elevators) - when clicks on any floor - call specic floors to create hallrequest - call controller to handle requests - use strategy to get bast Eleavtor
- delegate  request  to elevator - elevators take up the requests acts upon next request


user flow refined

1. User presses UP/DOWN button on a floor.
2. Floor creates a HallRequest.
3. Assigned elevator arrives at the floor.
4. User enters the elevator.
5. User selects destination floor.
6. Elevator creates a CabinRequest.
7. Elevator moves to the destination floor.
8. User exits the elevator.

Building
    ↓
User presses floor button
    ↓
Floor creates HallRequest
    ↓
ElevatorController receives request
    ↓
ElevatorAllocationStrategy selects best elevator
    ↓
Controller assigns request to selected elevator
    ↓
Elevator adds request to its pending queue
    ↓
Elevator executes requests one by one
    ↓
Passenger enters elevator
    ↓
Passenger selects destination floor
    ↓
Elevator creates CabinRequest
    ↓
Elevator adds destination to its pending queue
    ↓
Elevator continues executing requests